{"text": "Tissue culture of mammalian cells.\nTissue culture has been the key instrument in the investigation of cell biology. The advantages of the technique include (1) the possibility of obtaining large numbers of cells for experiments requiring the use of a large number of cells in the same sample; (2) the possibility of performing experiments in a controlled environment; and (3) the possibility of studying various aspects of cellular development under different conditions. This paper is an overview of the basic principles of tissue culture as well as a description of the basic cell culture methods and the experimental design for use in tissue culture. The advantages and disadvantages of the various tissue culture techniques are discussed. The authors hope that the paper will be of help to researchers in the field of cell biology. In addition, the basic steps in tissue culture techniques will be useful to students in their studies and to other scientists who wish to learn about tissue culture and its application in cell biology.", "depth": 3, "seed_id": 2, "token_count": 512}

